<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seonjo of Joseon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1552">1552</a>–<a href="/years/1608">1608</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seonjo was the fourteenth king of Joseon, ruling from 1567 to 1608. His reign saw a flowering of Neo-Confucian scholarship but also the split of officials into rival factions. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> invaded in 1592 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Seoul</a> fell, Seonjo fled north to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uiju">Uiju</a> on the Yalu and appealed to the Ming for help. The war of 1592–1598 devastated the country, and his reign was spent in recovering from it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seonjo-of-joseon.jpg" alt="Seonjo of Joseon" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 朝鮮画师 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%9C%9D%E9%AE%AE%E5%AE%A3%E7%A5%96.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
